[05:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'hit version two territory within months. Late August alone saw 2.6 and its patch on the 24th, 2.7 on the 27th and 2.8 on the 31st with the last commit landing hours before we filmed.'

[05:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Semantic release keeps the change logs honest and the pace shows no sign of cooling. The change log reads feature first. Real additions like the Plex integration and per user permissions. Not just dependency bumps. The honest'

[05:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'context, Oral is MIT licensed, properly free, no asterisks. The dependencies to know, it\'s a companion, so you need a working Lidarr first. This is the cherry on a stack, not the stack. Discovery'

[05:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'leans on hosted metadata from the Brainz Mash community service, so a piece of the recommendation pipeline lives outside your network. Downloading via YTDLP and Soulseek sits in the same legal gray zone as the rest'

[06:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'of the ARR world. Know your jurisdiction and your conscience. And it\'s a young, mostly one-person project moving very fast. Pin a version if you value stability, ride nightly if you don\'t. Owning your music was never supposed to mean freezing your'

